# BUG REPRO: #8944 over-drop on the ntp request tx — head-gap with a later BARE < rule.
#
# The ntp request tx is created at detect progress 0 (request_started) and
# completes within the same packet (the ntp parser is transactional:
# ntp_tx_get_alstate_progress always returns 1 — tx_progress 1,
# detect_progress_orig 0). The head candidate (accept:flow request_complete,
# hook 1) has a head-of-list gap (1 > 0) on the first detection pass, before
# the < rule has ever been inspected.
#
# The later accept:flow ntp:<request_complete rule legitimately covers the gap
# (bare rule, no keyword — it auto-accepts request_started and matches at
# completion). Correct behaviour: the request is accepted (no default app
# policy drop).
#
# main: "missing fw rules at list start: sid 852, progress 1 (1:0)" -> to_server
#   default app policy drop (over-drop, #8944 family — the ntp mirror of 221/222/223).
# bug-8944-new/v3: max_in_progress_lte_hook sees no stored state for the < rule
#   on the single-packet first pass -> same over-drop.
# the #8944 fix (firewall-bug-8944-new/v5): max_in_progress_lte_hook includes this-pass
# prefilter candidates (no stored state on the single-packet first pass) -> suppresses
# the gap -> accept (correct).
#
# Note: ntp is UDP-only and has two progress values per direction
# (request_started 0 / request_complete 1), so only the four generic app hooks
# exist (no per-state hook names). All ntp keywords (ntp.version/ntp.mode/
# ntp.stratum/ntp.reference_id) register at progress 1 with
# SIGMATCH_SUPPORT_FIREWALL (rust/src/ntp/detect.rs).
accept:hook udp:all 192.0.2.1 any <> 192.0.2.123 any (flow:not_established; sid:1021;)
accept:hook udp:all 192.0.2.1 any <> 192.0.2.123 any (flow:established; sid:1022;)
# bare head accept:flow at request_complete, followed by a later bare < rule
accept:flow ntp:request_complete 192.0.2.1 any -> 192.0.2.123 any (sid:852;)
accept:flow ntp:<request_complete 192.0.2.1 any -> 192.0.2.123 any (sid:853;)
# to_client shield (response states covered bare)
accept:hook ntp:response_started 192.0.2.123 any -> 192.0.2.1 any (sid:1003;)
accept:hook ntp:response_complete 192.0.2.123 any -> 192.0.2.1 any (sid:1004;)
